First, let's assign values to A, B, and C based on the ratio. Let A = 2x, B = x, and C = 4x. Then, (3A + 2B) = 3(2x) + 2(x) = 6x + 2x = 8x, and (4C - A) = 4(4x) - 2x = 16x - 2x = 14x. Therefore, (3A + 2B) ÷ (4C - A) = 8x ÷ 14x = \dfrac{8}{14} = \dfrac{4}{7}. </think> <answer>
\begin{align*}
\dfrac{4}{7}
\end{align*}

